  "statement": "When simplified the product \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\left(1-\\dfrac13\\right)\\left(1-\\dfrac14\\right)\\\\ &\\quad{}\\cdot\\left(1-\\dfrac15\\right)\\cdots\\left(1-\\dfrac1n\\right) \\end{aligned} \\] becomes:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac1n\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac2n\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{2(n-1)}n\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{n(n+1)}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{n(n+1)}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1959-p37.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The product telescopes: \\[ \\frac23\\cdot\\frac34\\cdot\\frac45\\cdots\\frac{n-1}{n} =\\frac2n. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
